WEBVTT

1
00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:54.000
In these verses of

2
00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.208
Chapter 11, a dramatic shift

3
00:00:57.208 --> 00:00:59.333
is seen in Arjun's emotions.

4
00:00:59.333 --> 00:01:02.125
Until now, his relationship with Lord Krishna

5
00:01:02.125 --> 00:01:04.875
had always been that of a dear friend.

6
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:05.333
But

7
00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.208
now he understands

8
00:01:07.208 --> 00:01:10.708
that out of ignorance, he had
treated the Supreme Lord

9
00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:13.708
with a familiarity

10
00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:17.250
that did not befit His divine stature.

11
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.000
And so he seeks forgiveness

12
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.375
for this error.

13
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:27.875
Overwhelmed by Lord Krishna's

14
00:01:27.875 --> 00:01:30.208
Vishwarupa,

15
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.875
Arjun now begins to grasp the depth

16
00:01:32.875 --> 00:01:34.541
of his former ignorance.

17
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:35.333
For years,

18
00:01:35.333 --> 00:01:37.958
Arjun had regarded Lord Krishna
only as a dear companion,

19
00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:39.166
addressing Him

20
00:01:39.166 --> 00:01:42.500
as 'Krishna' or 'Yadava',

21
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.583
unaware of the divinity residing within Him.

22
00:01:46.583 --> 00:01:49.208
Their relationship was one of closeness,

23
00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:51.000
filled with light-hearted banter

24
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.875
and casual conversation.

25
00:01:53.875 --> 00:01:54.958
But

26
00:01:54.958 --> 00:01:56.250
now, seeing Lord Krishna

27
00:01:56.250 --> 00:01:59.250
in His cosmic form, Arjun

28
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.666
feels shame about his past behaviour.

29
00:02:02.666 --> 00:02:05.125
He recalls the moments when,

30
00:02:05.125 --> 00:02:06.625
unaware of Lord Krishna's

31
00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:08.750
supreme nature,

32
00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.291
they sat together, ate together,

33
00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:14.750
and joked with each other

34
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.708
in private and in public.

35
00:02:16.708 --> 00:02:17.750
In deep humility,

36
00:02:17.750 --> 00:02:19.916
he seeks forgiveness,

37
00:02:19.916 --> 00:02:21.416
acknowledging

38
00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:23.875
that although his actions came from ignorance

39
00:02:23.875 --> 00:02:28.375
or affection, they were still improper.

40
00:02:28.375 --> 00:02:29.666
This shift in Arjun's

41
00:02:29.666 --> 00:02:32.750
perspective shows how realisation

42
00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:36.333
can transform one's understanding
of a relationship.

43
00:02:36.333 --> 00:02:38.500
Until now, he had seen Lord Krishna

44
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:40.583
as a dear companion.

45
00:02:40.583 --> 00:02:41.083
But

46
00:02:41.083 --> 00:02:44.166
now he sees Him as the Supreme Lord,

47
00:02:44.166 --> 00:02:46.375
and this realisation fills him

48
00:02:46.375 --> 00:02:49.666
with both reverence and remorse.

49
00:02:49.666 --> 00:02:52.541
Yet even in his apology,

50
00:02:52.541 --> 00:02:54.916
we see Lord Krishna's grace.

51
00:02:54.916 --> 00:02:56.750
He never took offence

52
00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.833
at Arjun's casual words.

53
00:02:58.833 --> 00:03:02.250
This reveals Lord Krishna's generosity.

54
00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:04.375
Even as the Supreme Lord,

55
00:03:04.375 --> 00:03:05.958
He maintains with His devotees

56
00:03:05.958 --> 00:03:09.958
an intimate, loving relationship,

57
00:03:09.958 --> 00:03:13.083
without ego or distance.

58
00:03:17.541 --> 00:03:20.666
Do you know

59
00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.791
that admitting a mistake

60
00:03:22.791 --> 00:03:26.333
is not weakness, but

61
00:03:26.333 --> 00:03:29.875
the greatest courage?

62
00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:34.541
When you make a mistake, what do you do?

63
00:03:34.541 --> 00:03:36.708
Do you ask for forgiveness,

64
00:03:36.708 --> 00:03:41.083
or do you stay stubborn?

65
00:03:41.083 --> 00:03:44.583
Look at Arjun.

66
00:03:44.583 --> 00:03:48.083
Even as a great warrior,

67
00:03:48.083 --> 00:03:51.500
when he recognised his error,

68
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.458
without hesitation

69
00:03:53.458 --> 00:03:56.625
he bowed his head and sought forgiveness.

70
00:03:56.625 --> 00:03:58.583
Mistakes

71
00:03:58.583 --> 00:04:03.583
are part of life.

72
00:04:03.583 --> 00:04:06.166
What matters is this:

73
00:04:06.166 --> 00:04:09.625
when you recognise a mistake,

74
00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:11.541
what do you do?

75
00:04:11.541 --> 00:04:13.916
Many people fear

76
00:04:13.916 --> 00:04:17.291
that if they apologise,

77
00:04:17.291 --> 00:04:20.208
they will appear weak.

78
00:04:20.208 --> 00:04:22.333
But do you know

79
00:04:22.333 --> 00:04:25.625
what true strength is?

80
00:04:25.625 --> 00:04:29.291
Admitting when you are wrong.

81
00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:31.708
When you sincerely

82
00:04:31.708 --> 00:04:34.791
accept your mistake,

83
00:04:34.791 --> 00:04:36.833
what happens?

84
00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:39.875
You open the path to improvement

85
00:04:39.875 --> 00:04:44.083
and stronger relationships,

86
00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:47.791
whether the mistake is small or large.

87
00:04:47.791 --> 00:04:49.625
Remember,

88
00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:50.666
seeking forgiveness

89
00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:53.583
does not make you small.

90
00:04:53.583 --> 00:04:58.666
It elevates your character

91
00:04:58.666 --> 00:05:00.875
and gives you the strength

92
00:05:00.875 --> 00:05:04.333
to move forward with clarity.

93
00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:13.333
Closeness in a home is good.

94
00:05:13.333 --> 00:05:15.958
But can too much familiarity

95
00:05:15.958 --> 00:05:19.208
sometimes become a problem?

96
00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:21.375
Look at Arjun.

97
00:05:21.375 --> 00:05:24.416
After seeing My cosmic form,

98
00:05:24.416 --> 00:05:26.958
Arjun realised that he

99
00:05:26.958 --> 00:05:31.583
had been too casual with Me,

100
00:05:31.583 --> 00:05:35.166
as one would be with an ordinary friend.

101
00:05:35.166 --> 00:05:39.625
Do you perhaps do the same?

102
00:05:39.625 --> 00:05:41.333
When family members

103
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:44.333
speak to you with love,

104
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:47.375
do you forget to respect them?

105
00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:49.250
Understand,

106
00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:53.666
closeness is natural in family relationships,

107
00:05:53.666 --> 00:05:55.541
but what is the harm

108
00:05:55.541 --> 00:06:00.041
of too much familiarity?

109
00:06:00.041 --> 00:06:03.125
A feeling of disrespect creeps in.

110
00:06:03.125 --> 00:06:04.500
For example,

111
00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:09.416
the contributions of parents begin
to be overlooked.

112
00:06:09.416 --> 00:06:12.791
You speak without thinking.

113
00:06:12.791 --> 00:06:16.458
You stop caring about their feelings.

114
00:06:16.458 --> 00:06:19.250
Now how to avoid this?

115
00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:24.000
Simply do this: keep your closeness,

116
00:06:24.000 --> 00:06:28.791
but never let respect diminish.

117
00:06:28.791 --> 00:06:33.625
Keep saying 'thank you' and 'I respect you.'

118
00:06:33.625 --> 00:06:35.708
Keep saying it,

119
00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:38.125
laugh and joke,

120
00:06:38.125 --> 00:06:42.250
but do not cross the line of dignity,

121
00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:47.375
and acknowledge each other's efforts.

122
00:06:47.375 --> 00:06:49.250
Remember,

123
00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.208
true closeness

124
00:06:51.208 --> 00:06:55.958
comes from both love and respect.

125
00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:58.666
Keeping these in mind

126
00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:02.250
will strengthen your relationships

127
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:05.416
and deepen your love.

128
00:07:09.833 --> 00:07:12.333
Do you know

129
00:07:12.333 --> 00:07:17.250
that admitting a mistake at
work is not weakness,

130
00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.708
but the greatest strength?

131
00:07:20.708 --> 00:07:25.375
When you make a mistake,

132
00:07:25.375 --> 00:07:28.541
what do you do?

133
00:07:28.541 --> 00:07:30.375
Do you hide it,

134
00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:33.791
or openly admit it?

135
00:07:33.791 --> 00:07:37.375
Look at Arjun.

136
00:07:37.375 --> 00:07:41.541
When he understood My divine nature,

137
00:07:41.541 --> 00:07:45.458
he immediately admitted his mistake.

138
00:07:45.458 --> 00:07:49.625
This is true integrity.

139
00:07:49.625 --> 00:07:51.791
Understand this:

140
00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:55.041
everyone makes mistakes,

141
00:07:55.041 --> 00:07:56.875
but in such moments,

142
00:07:56.875 --> 00:08:02.666
what does a successful professional do?

143
00:08:02.666 --> 00:08:07.041
They take responsibility for them

144
00:08:07.041 --> 00:08:09.375
and learn from them.

145
00:08:09.375 --> 00:08:13.208
When you admit a mistake,

146
00:08:13.208 --> 00:08:15.833
what happens?

147
00:08:15.833 --> 00:08:19.500
It shows your integrity.

148
00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.125
Colleagues and seniors

149
00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:26.875
begin to respect you.

150
00:08:26.875 --> 00:08:28.500
But

151
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:31.583
if you hide mistakes

152
00:08:31.583 --> 00:08:34.541
or blame others,

153
00:08:34.541 --> 00:08:39.958
that is only a temporary solution.

154
00:08:39.958 --> 00:08:41.458
But

155
00:08:41.458 --> 00:08:43.416
in the long run,

156
00:08:43.416 --> 00:08:47.333
your credibility is lost.

157
00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:49.208
So what should you do?

158
00:08:49.208 --> 00:08:52.708
See mistakes as opportunities to learn,

159
00:08:52.708 --> 00:08:58.875
and from that very moment,
take steps toward improvement.

160
00:08:58.875 --> 00:09:02.541
So think about what went wrong.

161
00:09:02.541 --> 00:09:05.000
Make the necessary changes,

162
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:10.458
and keep striving to become better.

163
00:09:10.458 --> 00:09:12.833
Reflect on this.

164
00:09:12.833 --> 00:09:14.916
This approach not only

165
00:09:14.916 --> 00:09:19.250
builds your skill, but also

166
00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:22.166
develops at the workplace

167
00:09:22.166 --> 00:09:27.750
a culture of openness and continuous learning.
